From cfcc637b0f97188227f3810caf9d7d0068fb7131 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:50:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] chore(secrets): reword observed.rs:101 so the secrets gate
 passes (pr/61)

gitleaks (8.30.1) flagged observed.rs:101 under generic-api-key: a comment
reading "used as a key: <dated model id>", a false positive. Reworded the
comment; no allowlist change.
---
 crates/toolpath-goldens/src/observed.rs |  2 +-
 pr/61-secrets-gate-clean.md             | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 pr/61-secrets-gate-clean.md

diff --git a/crates/toolpath-goldens/src/observed.rs b/crates/toolpath-goldens/src/observed.rs
index 2264b120..38a89836 100644
--- a/crates/toolpath-goldens/src/observed.rs
+++ b/crates/toolpath-goldens/src/observed.rs
@@ -98,7 +98,7 @@ fn data_key(k: &str) -> bool {
     k.contains('/')
         || k.len() > 40
         || (k.len() >= 16 && k.chars().all(|c| c.is_ascii_hexdigit() || c == '-'))
-        // a dated model id used as a key: `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001`
+        // a dated model id (`claude-haiku-4-5-20251001`) used as a key
         || digit_run >= 8
 }
 
diff --git a/pr/61-secrets-gate-clean.md b/pr/61-secrets-gate-clean.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..6c21774a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/pr/61-secrets-gate-clean.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# chore(secrets): reword observed.rs:101 so the secrets gate passes on wip
+
+Status: draft · Base: pr/59-secrets-gate-placeholders · One comment line; no allowlist change
+
+## Why
+`scripts/quality_gates.sh secrets` (gitleaks 8.30.1, from the wip dev shell) still found one leak after pr/59:
+crates/toolpath-goldens/src/observed.rs:101, rule `generic-api-key`. The comment ended in "used as a key", a colon, then a
+dated Claude model id in backticks, which reads as `key: <value>`. The value is a public model id, not a credential — a
+false positive. (Not quoted verbatim here: quoted, it makes this record the finding.)
+
+## What changes
+- observed.rs:101: the comment now puts the model id in parentheses before "used as a key", so no `key:` precedes it.
+  Comment only; no code changed.
+
+## Not changed
+- .gitleaks.toml: changing the string was preferred to widening the allowlist.
+
+## Checked
+- `gitleaks dir . --config .gitleaks.toml --redact`: no leaks found.
-- 
